{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/40000-musings-on-a-new-wraith","id":40000,"title":"Musings on a new Wraith","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-31T08:11:17-08:00","id":40000,"title":"Musings on a new Wraith","content":"Recently, I've had some musings on how a new Wraith might work in the nWoD, specially after having read Mummy, Geist (finally), God Machine Chronicles and Blood &amp; Smoke.<br /> <br /> Here's how I would do it in a way that mashes well with other games (specially Geist, because you can't ignore it) and reinforces it's themes. Just doing it for fun.<br /> <br /> I remember reading in one book (might be misremembering) that ghosts don't have souls. The ghost is the energy that stays, but the soul goes away, no one knows where to.<br /> <br /> Then, a Wraith is what happens when the soul stays with the ghost. It's rare, but it does happen.<br /> <br /> Losing the body, though, has an effect on the mind of the individual. It is not as contained as it was. As the mind is not confined by the limits of the brain, it might fragment, grow in stranger ways. It is easy to lose it's sense of identity. <br /> <br /> So, the main power stat of the Wraith is still Psyche, like in Geist. And the fuel is also Plasm.<br /> <br /> Morality/Integrity is replaced by Memory, like in Mummy. However, a Wraith starts with Memory 7. They also have anchors, that work like Touchstones. However, a Wraith has an Anchor for each level of Memory and don't attach it to specific levels of Memory. When losing Memory, player choses which Anchor he loses. Once an Anchor is gone, it's gone for good. Players can't get new Anchors, but instead may buy (Like a Touchstone merit) a Fetter.<br /> <br /> Anchor: Anchors are related to the Wraith's life and are specific. People (my wife), objects (the knife that killed me), places (the house of my childhood). When an Anchor is destroyed, the Wraith loses a dot of Memory.<br /> <br /> Fetter: Fetters are related to the Wraith's death and are not specific. Objects (knifes), places (alleyways like the one I died), feelings (hatred). You can't have more Fetters then your Psyche. Also, Fetters change the Wraith's appearance in some way. (knifed fingers, bloodied steps, red eyes with steam coming from them).<br /> <br /> When you have more Fetters then Anchors, you lose your name and chose a new, more archetypical one. You might still remember the old name, but you don't resonate with it anymore. You start resonating with the Archetypical one.<br /> <br /> Some new Memory sins:<br /> <br /> 7 - Doing your Shadow conditions (dirge) or Aspirations.<br /> 6 - Not using your own name (remember who you are) - This is not a Sin once you have more Fetters then Anchors.<br /> 5 - Using your own name - Once you have more Fetters then Anchors.<br /> 4 - a week without talking with other ghosts, or without seeing an anchor (Et in Arcadia Ego)<br /> 3 - Interacting directly with the living (remember, you're dead)<br /> 2 - Pretending to be alive (remember, you died)<br /> <br /> Wraiths have a Threshold, like in Geist.<br /> <br /> Self and Shadow: Work like Mask and Dirge from Blood &amp; Smoke, respectively. However, Self is your ideal self, how you think you should act. Shadow is against it, how you don't think you should react (It's not necessarily bad. It's just against who you think you are. An Authoritarian might have Jester as a Shadow. You think you have to be a hard man, but man\u2026 those jokes just keep coming in your head. They won't respect you if you tell the joke, but you're witty. It might escape!).<br /> <br /> Keys: Given by the Threshold, like in Geist. they might determine the types of Numina the Wraith can get. Firestarter is Pyre-Flame, for instance (this might need some work, still).<br /> <br /> Aspirations: Wraiths choose Two Aspirations, like normal, and a third, Shadow Aspiration. This is related to his Shadow Archetype. They also chose two Resolutions. They are major things that need to resolve of their deaths, and are related to one of his Anchors (help my wife move on, revenge on my killer, get the house of my childhood back to my family). When you resolve, you lose that specific Anchor (and a dot of Memory). However, when you fulfill a Resolution, and it was your last Anchor, you get to transcend! Whatever that means. :P<br /> <br /> Getting Plasm:<br /> <br /> Every time someone mention your name (the one you resonate with), or remember you died, next to you, roll Resolve + Composure + Psyche.<br /> <br /> When next to an Anchor or Fetter, you roll Resolve + Composure + Psyche. You can only do it once a day.<br /> <br /> That way, for it to gain Plasm, the Wraith has to remind people of it's death in some way. Perhaps next to his wife, he uses Telekinesis to knock his portrait so that she has to get it from the floor. When he is more Archetypical, he might have to create an urban legend in some way. (&quot;I heard that the ghost of Knife-hands stalks these alleyways and kills everyone that has too much rage in their hearts!&quot;)<br /> <br /> You fill your plasm when you fulfill a Resolution.<br /> <br /> Shadow Experience: Fulfilling a Shadow Aspiration and Getting a bead by getting a Dramatic Failure instead of a Failure gives Shadow Beads and Experience. It can be used to buy Fetters and Psyche.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is it, in a nutshell. Loved the Stygian parts in the old Wraith, so I would probably do something like that. Perhaps some places in the Underworld that only the TRULY dead can enter. <br /> <br /> Also, a Wraith with more fetters then Anchor is, for all intends and purposes, a Geist.<br /> <br /> Opinions, suggestions, anything? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T16:24:49-08:00","id":40203,"title":"","content":"Overall, I like it. I\u2019d do a few things differently, myself\u2026<br /> <br /> A minor bit of renaming: Eidolon instead of Self. Eidolon was a Background in <b>Wraith: the Oblivion</b> that represented the wraith\u2019s \u201chigher self\u201d. <br /> <br /> I\u2019d make wraiths more desparate. A wraith is a ghost that has had the spark of life reignited in him, possibly right after his death and possibly after centuries languishing as a ghost; but while that means that he is once again a full person instead of merely a remnant of one, it comes at the cost of burning through his life (adapt the rules for Sekhem loss for this purpose; but apply it to Memory). When they lose their last dot of Memory, they succumb to Oblivion and cease to exist. <br /> <br /> They have the ability to stave off Oblivion by indulging their Passions. Passions are Conditions, except that the beats of experience earned are dedicated to buying dots of Memory. Passions also interact with Eidolon and Shadow: indulging in a Passion while satisfying your Eidolon lets you regain all of your Plasm as well as all of your Willpower (once per story); doing so while indulgng in your Shadow earns you a single point of Plasm (once per scene) \u2014 or you can forgo the \u201cMemory Beat\u201d and refill your Plasm instead. Passions themselves are neither good nor bad; it\u2019s all a matter of the end to which you apply them. Each Passion that you Resolve brings you one step closer to Transcendence; but it also removes one of your bulwarks against Oblivion. <br /> <br /> A wraith doesn\u2019t have an Anchor for each level of Memory; he has an Anchor for each Passion. Resolving the Passion eliminates the Anchor associated with it; Anchors are not themselves Resolved. <br /> <br /> I\u2019d have Aspirations work like they do for mortals: no division between \u201cgood Aspirations\u201d and \u201cbad Aspirations\u201d. <br /> <br /> I like the idea of organizing a wraith\u2019s Numina by Key, or at least by Threshold. <br /> <br /> I also like the \u201cbecome a geist\u201d option, though I\u2019d treat it as a sort of Threshold-based z-splat and I wouldn\u2019t use Fetters: once you have sufficient Psyche, you can choose to bind yourself to some aspect of death that resonates with your Threshold; doing so interferes with (or outright prevents?) your ability to Transcend, but also immunizes you from Oblivion: once you lose all of your Memory, you become an Unfettered Geist. It also grants you Influence over that aspect of Death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T05:12:45-08:00","id":40466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Max Deltree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/40000-musings-on-a-new-wraith#post40000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember reading in one book (might be misremembering) that ghosts don't have souls. The ghost is the energy that stays, but the soul goes away, no one knows where to.</div> </div> </div> </div> You are misremembering, it never says either way.<br /> <br /> Mage's say they don't IC, but that's a controversial position and other Mages say it's just a justification for Ghost slavery.<br /> <br /> Geist dosn't say at all. Though I spoke with one author who believes they do (and that Geist as a game dosn't work if they don't)<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, now I've read it, the concept seems like a starting point but it's too early for me to really say much. Personally for me I'd be interested in really keeping it simple. You're actually playing the semi-aware Ghosts you meet in Geist; since I suspect that's not the goal here I wont say more/","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 01-01-2014, 08:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T11:59:57-08:00","id":41226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/40000-musings-on-a-new-wraith?p=40203#post40203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Overall, I like it. I\u2019d do a few things differently, myself\u2026<br /> <br /> I\u2019d make wraiths more desparate. A wraith is a ghost that has had the spark of life reignited in him, possibly right after his death and possibly after centuries languishing as a ghost; but while that means that he is once again a full person instead of merely a remnant of one, it comes at the cost of burning through his life (adapt the rules for Sekhem loss for this purpose; but apply it to Memory). When they lose their last dot of Memory, they succumb to Oblivion and cease to exist.<br /> <br /> They have the ability to stave off Oblivion by indulging their Passions. Passions are Conditions, except that the beats of experience earned are dedicated to buying dots of Memory. Passions also interact with Eidolon and Shadow: indulging in a Passion while satisfying your Eidolon lets you regain all of your Plasm as well as all of your Willpower (once per story); doing so while indulgng in your Shadow earns you a single point of Plasm (once per scene) \u2014 or you can forgo the \u201cMemory Beat\u201d and refill your Plasm instead. Passions themselves are neither good nor bad; it\u2019s all a matter of the end to which you apply them. Each Passion that you Resolve brings you one step closer to Transcendence; but it also removes one of your bulwarks against Oblivion.</div> </div> </div> </div>My main problem is that this is too close to the theme of the old W:tO game, might as well make a Wraith20 rather than a nWoD version of Wraith.<br /> <br /> Overall I like the ideas in the original post, especially the need for Wraiths to interact with humans in order to regain Plasm. I might be tempted to add a &quot;dark side / quick and dirty&quot; method for getting Plasm from mortals similar to how Strix gain Vitae. This should help cause memory loss and further the Wraith's transition from actualized person to otherworldly thing. At Memory 0 they become a Spectre, which is the Wraith equivalent to a Draugr. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T17:01:40-08:00","id":41402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> My main problem is that this is too close to the theme of the old W:tO game, might as well make a Wraith20 rather than a nWoD version of Wraith.<br /> <br /> Overall I like the ideas in the original post, especially the need for Wraiths to interact with humans in order to regain Plasm. I might be tempted to add a &quot;dark side / quick and dirty&quot; method for getting Plasm from mortals similar to how Strix gain Vitae. This should help cause memory loss and further the Wraith's transition from actualized person to otherworldly thing. At Memory 0 they become a Spectre, which is the Wraith equivalent to a Draugr.</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked the Old Wraith game, (THB I liked Orpheus better), and I am looking forward W20 which we were promised by Onyx Path. (I think it's after Mage).<br /> But I won't do it a diservice by trying to re-create it in the nWoD. The settings are too different. While nWoD is a toolbox and you could just toss out all the contradictions, I feel that is a waste of potential. I'd rather take the best elements of the old and use this 'new' toolbox to bring them across.<br /> <br /> I posted in the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/40901-wraiths-as-minor-ish-template?p=41391#post41391\">other thread</a> some ideas that may help differentiate the concepts while still leaving it playable. It's not much but it should help remind us that we shouldn't try to reinvent the wheel, we should be trying to use it to build something better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T17:47:31-08:00","id":41423,"title":"","content":"Eh. This has about as much in common with <b>Wraith: the Oblivion</b> as <b>Mage: the Awakening</b> has with <b>Mage: the Ascension</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T18:49:26-08:00","id":41444,"title":"","content":"True, but Oblivion has more dramatic pull than Ascension. Imperial Mysteries proves that.<br /> Likewise while either of the metaphysics for Ascension work regardless of if you are using the systems for M:Ac or M:Aw, Oblivion doesn't have that flexibility.<br /> At the end of the day, it's still <b><i><u>Oblivion</u></i></b>, the end of everything and destruction. Wraith, Orpheus and Exalted ended up using it in the same role and it's hard not too.<br /> <br /> I just think that of all the things we can take from Wraith, a bottomless pit which drives you (without mind control) into <i>nihilistic insanity</i> is not the best choice. And even if we internalize it, that second part is still problematic.<br /> <br /> Plus Mage are the lines closest to each other, so they aren't the best comparison for your point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T20:51:17-08:00","id":41494,"title":"","content":"Prior to B&amp;S, Vampire were the lines closest to each other. If you go into any depth at all, the two Mage games differ from each other drastically. <br /> <br /> And where did I say anything about nihilistic insanity? That\u2019s not what I picture when I speak of Oblivion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-02-2014, 11:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T16:58:58-08:00","id":42037,"title":"","content":"I never said you did and I am sorry if it feels like putting words in your mouth so to speak.<br /> <br /> I guess it's my fault that 'Oblivion' has become such a loaded term for me. Too many memories of Wraith and Orpheus. Good ones, but ...<br /> <br /> I am aware that the Mage settings are quite different, but what I was trying to say is that Ascension plays the same narrative role in path, albeit downplayed in M;tAw. Using Oblivion, even in the vastly different mechanical form you've described, ties into my own memories of it's use in previous games. As I realized, it's a problem with my mindset, not yours.<br /> <br /> As for nihilistic insanity...it was a rationale for Spectres. Self-loathing only goes so far. That said, while not as 'bad' as derangement, Memory loss can include various Conditions. For the sake of sanity, let's only get them at breaking points, not automatic losses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T22:42:12-08:00","id":46086,"title":"","content":"I agree with that sentiment.<br /> <br /> Actually, I like the idea that Oblivion deserves to be treated as a neutral force. It isn't the sponsor of the Shadow, the Shadow doesn't want to become nonexistent, and indeed might be more interesting in Transcending than the Eidolon is, if the Eidolon is particularly materialistic.<br /> <br /> I do think the Power of the Void needs to be an antagonistic force to Wraiths though. Perhaps it can and does produce true spirits (with Influences and sans Virtue/Vice) as a response to the discomfort of wraiths constantly straining against it by existing. These are sort of like the Strix, in that they're a constant thorn in the side of wraith society, but unlike the Strix, the Reapers (though a better name would probably be Psychopomps) don't hate wraiths. They don't hate much of anything, or feel care about anything-they're completely detached from everything except their Passions, even their own self-awareness (thus, they're known for nigh-suicidal bravery, as they don't feel fear of death, only of failure). Their primary purpose is to cut Anchors and make the wraiths either accept Oblivion or Transcend as soon as possible, and to regulate death in the living world. <br /> <br /> And yes, this makes them sound like angels. They aren't, but the two get along pretty well when they occasionally encounter each other. Or not. It depends on the Mission and the Passion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T16:54:28-08:00","id":46591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/40000-musings-on-a-new-wraith?p=46086#post46086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It isn't the sponsor of the Shadow, the Shadow doesn't want to become nonexistent, and indeed might be more interesting in Transcending than the Eidolon is, if the Eidolon is particularly materialistic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always thought that it's more logical for the Shadow to be an extreme version of the wraith's passions - her passions might make up a lot of her identity, but they make up the <i>whole</i> of the shadow's, it can think of nothing else - thus being overwhelmed by the shadow means ending up like regular ghosts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do think the Power of the Void needs to be an antagonistic force to Wraiths though. Perhaps it can and does produce true spirits </div> </div> </div>The chthonians could be such a thing (though they don't really rally with the rest of your idea, except inasmuch as sineaters don't know what they hell they are).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}